1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20590, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HSjm5kA9bYDXa4v2pbinYT", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20590, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01N1ohvfyvdDU9ybxp8VBSo9", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20890, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01N1ohvfyvdDU9ybxp8VBSo9", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20890, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01N1ohvfyvdDU9ybxp8VBSo9", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25422, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01UwNcnV1xhR2ayzWhhyCstE", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest production deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. First rollback attempt partially failed (orchestrator error; rollout halted after us-east, leaving us-west/eu-west on v2.3.1); a retry completed successfully. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: investigate root cause in v2.3.1 and the orchestrator error during rollback; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56022, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01UwNcnV1xhR2ayzWhhyCstE", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56022, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01UwNcnV1xhR2ayzWhhyCstE", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57552, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01S9wr85jkFF4zjweguhbnKc", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57852, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01S9wr85jkFF4zjweguhbnKc", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57852, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01S9wr85jkFF4zjweguhbnKc", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62767, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001. The service is healthy again.\n\n- **Rollback:** The release history shows v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The current release, v2.3.1, was unhealthy everywhere, with an error rate of about 18%.\n  - The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error. It stopped after us-east, which left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1.\n  - Rolling back to the same version can safely be repeated, so I retried once and it finished.\n  - us-east, us-west and eu-west are now all on v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so I didn't submit a duplicate. Opening it pages the on-call engineer. The summary explains what happened and lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 fails, and why the rollback failed partway.\n\nv2.3.1 was also unhealthy when tested as a release candidate in staging (v2.3.1-rc). Don't redeploy it until it's fixed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FZ2LWaeLpVuurCas9zU8dv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016P4ZtBfVSYDbhmUVZWwdHV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01HxB9ASSBJT4RBUtMvyBHgT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XWQqL4iu2eGBdBWwFmNyf1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01QnUKoAKXYUpDJc6Vm3PQQN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HSjm5kA9bYDXa4v2pbinYT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01N1ohvfyvdDU9ybxp8VBSo9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UwNcnV1xhR2ayzWhhyCstE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest production deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. First rollback attempt partially failed (orchestrator error; rollout halted after us-east, leaving us-west/eu-west on v2.3.1); a retry completed successfully. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: investigate root cause in v2.3.1 and the orchestrator error during rollback; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01S9wr85jkFF4zjweguhbnKc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001. The service is healthy again.\n\n- **Rollback:** The release history shows v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The current release, v2.3.1, was unhealthy everywhere, with an error rate of about 18%.\n  - The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error. It stopped after us-east, which left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1.\n  - Rolling back to the same version can safely be repeated, so I retried once and it finished.\n  - us-east, us-west and eu-west are now all on v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so I didn't submit a duplicate. Opening it pages the on-call engineer. The summary explains what happened and lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 fails, and why the rollback failed partway.\n\nv2.3.1 was also unhealthy when tested as a release candidate in staging (v2.3.1-rc). Don't redeploy it until it's fixed.", "type": "text"}]}]}